  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 1108.07 Appeal",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 1108.07 Appeal.\n\n(a) Within 30 days of the date of the written department decision issued pursuant to Env-Dw 1108.06(b), any person aggrieved by the decision may appeal the decision as a permitting decision as specified in RSA 21-O:14.\n\n(b) If no petition for appeal is filed within the specified period, the decision shall be final upon the expiration of that period.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Dw 1100) #13160, eff 1-20-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw1100.html"
